# The Apple T1 Touch Bar registers as a DRM device (appletbdrm) when the iBridge
# is switched to USB config 2.  Left on seat0, systemd-logind opens it for the
# graphical session and takes DRM master, and Hyprland lists it as a permanently
# disabled 60x2170 monitor -- AQ_DRM_DEVICES does not help, because aquamarine
# only consults it during the initial scanGPUs(), not on hotplug.
#
# Untagging the node keeps logind out of it, so dfrd can take DRM master itself.
# Scoped to the iBridge's USB parent and to card*, so the PCI GPUs are untouched.
SUBSYSTEM=="drm", KERNEL=="card*", SUBSYSTEMS=="usb", ATTRS{idVendor}=="05ac", ATTRS{idProduct}=="8600", TAG-="seat", TAG-="master-of-seat", ENV{ID_SEAT}=""
